  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Governance and Democratic Participation Programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Governance and Democratic Participation Programme (GDPP) is a five-year, multi-stakeholder programme managed by the United Nations Development Programme (UNDP) and implemented by 11 institutions of the Government of Ethiopia (GoE). The main objective of the programme is to support Ethiopia sustain reform efforts towards enhancing institutional capacities and frameworks for strengthening good governance and deepening democratic participation.</narrative>
  </description>
